3. Commercial use and revenue. Commercial use means using the SDK or runtime
for commercial advantage or compensation, including internal business use.
Noncommercial use is free of the donation and enterprise licensing requirements.
For those requirements, calculate total annual revenue from all sources of the
user and its controlling, controlled, or commonly controlled entities on a
consolidated basis for the fiscal year, excluding intercompany transactions.
Control means the power to direct an entity's management and policies. Convert
revenue reported in other currencies to USD using the published central bank
exchange rate on the fiscal year-end date or the most recent prior date for
which one is available. Use an appropriately documented market rate when no
such central bank rate is available.

4. Donation. If you use the Work commercially during a fiscal year in which
your total annual revenue exceeds US$10,000, donate at least US$50 to a
qualifying project within 90 days after the end of that fiscal year. Repeat this
for each fiscal year that qualifies. A qualifying project uses a license approved
by the Open Source Initiative and has been public on GitHub for at least one
year with at least 1,000 organic stars at the time of donation. Make a good-faith
assessment and exclude stars you know were bought, traded, or generated by
bots. Use a donation or sponsorship channel designated by the project and retain
the receipt and the repository URL. This obligation also applies when enterprise
licensing is required under section 5.

5. Enterprise license. If the total annual revenue for your latest completed
fiscal year is US$10,000,000 or more, this license does not authorize commercial
use. To begin or continue commercial use, obtain a separate paid enterprise
license from the DIM copyright holder before doing so. The enterprise agreement
sets the fee and payment terms.

6. Termination. Your permissions under this license end if you fail to comply
with its terms. Permissions for downstream recipients who remain in compliance
continue. The disclaimer and limitation of liability survive termination.

7. Warranty and liability. The Work is provided as is, without warranties of
any kind, to the extent permitted by applicable law. To the extent permitted by
